# Slow gate — the API suite, plus a typecheck the pre-commit hook may never
# have run (a `--no-verify` commit, a commit made by another tool, a rebase).
#
# The web suite is not here. It is jsdom-bound and took ~4m54s of every push
# on a Windows dev machine (~4x slower than ubuntu-latest; see
# docs/standards/testing.md), and CI runs it on every PR anyway. CLAUDE.md
# makes a green PR the finish line, so CI owns it. The API suite stays: it is
# fast enough to pay per push, and it is the one that exercises the database.
#
# Measured 2026-09-24 on a Windows dev machine, warm: typecheck ~16s,
# `@ticket/api` ~33s — under a minute. A cold first run takes about twice that.
#
# E2E is not here either. It needs a Postgres, a migrated ticket_manager_test
# and two servers on alt ports (SCRIPTS.md); CI's `e2e` job owns it.
bun run typecheck
bun run --filter @ticket/api test
